# Email Spam Detection System using Machine Learning

## Overview

This project is a Machine Learning-based Email/SMS Spam Detection System developed using Python. The system classifies incoming messages as either **Spam** or **Ham (Not Spam)** using Natural Language Processing (NLP) techniques and a Logistic Regression classifier.

The model is trained on a labeled dataset containing spam and ham messages. Text data is converted into numerical features using **TF-IDF (Term Frequency-Inverse Document Frequency)** vectorization, enabling the machine learning model to understand and classify text effectively.

A user-friendly **Tkinter GUI** is integrated into the project, allowing users to paste any email or message and instantly determine whether it is spam or legitimate.

## Features

* Data preprocessing and cleaning
* Handling missing values
* Label encoding (Spam = 0, Ham = 1)
* TF-IDF text vectorization
* Logistic Regression classification
* Model accuracy evaluation
* Interactive Tkinter graphical user interface
* Real-time spam prediction for user-entered messages

## Technologies Used

* Python
* Pandas
* NumPy
* Scikit-learn
* Tkinter
* Natural Language Processing (NLP)

## Machine Learning Workflow

1. Load and preprocess the dataset.
2. Handle missing values.
3. Encode categorical labels.
4. Split data into training and testing sets.
5. Convert text into TF-IDF feature vectors.
6. Train a Logistic Regression model.
7. Evaluate model performance using accuracy metrics.
8. Predict whether a user-entered message is spam or ham through the GUI.

## Model Performance

The trained model achieves approximately:

* Training Accuracy: ~96.7%
* Testing Accuracy: ~96.6%

These results indicate strong generalization performance on unseen messages.

## Usage

1. Run the Python application.
2. Enter or paste an email/message into the text area.
3. Click the **Check Spam** button.
4. The system will display:

   * Spam Mail or Ham Mail
   * Model Accuracy

